{
  "reviews": {
    "node-1xs245x": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'No evidence confirms whether U-A/U-B used a different version or saw recent changes.' While the training extract lacks this information (source: IA-S03), the incident description and shift log do not establish that these operators were exposed to any specific configuration drawing at all. The claim conflates 'lack of briefing record' with 'no evidence they used/were aware of a different version'. Without an explicit statement in the supplied records about which drawings or versions U-A/U-B consulted, we cannot assert this proposition is fully supported; it remains partially-supported only because one source (training extract) lacks data. The missing premise is: does any other record state that no drawing was seen? If not, the claim overstates what is known.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A statement from a work folder cover or briefing log indicating whether U-A/U-B were issued or consulted any configuration drawings (and if so, which revision) at issue time. Alternatively, an explicit note that no drawing was provided to them.","question":"Does the WO-527 work package or daily briefing record state whether operators U-A and U-B received a specific configuration drawing for 1SC dryer maintenance?"
    },
    "node-1xb835e": {
      "supported": true,
      "issue": "",
      "evidenceNeeded": "","question":""
    },
    "node-j6clft": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node states 'The area directory (IA-D01) is a location index and does not establish valve positions or pressure availability at any given time.' This proposition is supported by IA-D01's own text. However, the node label omits that this limitation applies to all times including incident time; it also implies no other record can fill that gap without stating so. The claim as written conflates 'directory does not establish' with 'no evidence exists for valve state'. Since we have no positive evidence of valve states (only negative statements about what records do), the node should be labeled partially-supported rather than fully supported, because it asserts a fact ('does not establish') that is true but then implies an evidentiary gap without explicitly stating that other sources are absent. The missing premise: does any record affirmatively state valve positions or pressures at 10:00? If none exist, the node's 'supported' status should be downgraded to reflect that we only know what records do not show.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A positive measurement log (PLC trend, pressure gauge reading) for P-R at ~10:00 or a statement from an operator confirming valve positions. If none exist, document the absence explicitly rather than inferring it from record limitations.","question":"Is there any PLC trend, pressure gauge snapshot, or operator note that records instrument-air pressure at RHOB (P-R) around 10:00 on May 20?"
    }
  },
  "decision": {
    "summary": "Two nodes require status adjustment. Node-1xs245x overstates the lack of evidence about drawing usage; it should be partially-supported pending a record that either shows which drawings were issued or explicitly states none were provided. Node-j6clft is fully supported in its statement but mischaracterized as 'supported' without acknowledging the evidentiary gap for actual valve/pressure state at incident time; downgrade to partially-supported and request positive pressure data.",
    "evidenceUsed": ["IA-S03 (training extract lacks drawing info)", "IA-D01 (directory self-describes limitations)", "incident-description (no source of interruption identified)"],
    "unknowns": [
      "Whether U-A/U-B received any configuration drawings for 1SC maintenance.",
      "Actual instrument-air pressure at RHOB P-R around 10:00 on May 20."
    ],
    "alternatives": [
      "The air interruption originated upstream (site header) and was not captured in local records; thus valve states are irrelevant to the cause but still unknown.",
      "A service-routing change occurred without documentation, which would explain a blank attachment field but requires positive evidence of such a change."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.85
  }
}
